          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "தூண் — tūṇ — \"a pillar\"."
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "கோயிலின் தூண்களில் அழகான சிலைகள் இருக்கின்றன. kōyiliṉ tūṇkaḷil aḻakāṉa cilaikaḷ irukkiṉṟaṉa. There are beautiful statues on the temple pillars."
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "Plural: தூண்கள், tūṇkaḷ."
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "The plural is தூண்கள். கம்பம் (kampam) is a thinner post or pole."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 2,
          "type": "etymology",
          "title": "The word, taken apart",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "தூண் (tūṇ) stands in DEDR's appendix of words shared with Indo-Aryan (DEDR App. 44), beside Sanskrit sthūṇā, \"a post, a pillar\" (CDIAL 13774); which way the word travelled is not settled."
            }
          ]
        },
